LOCAL1="CoolerControl from its own makefile"
LOCAL2="A copy of CoolerControl made by upstream's makefile (%s) is on this computer, and the package coolercontrold is installed beside it. The package left your copy exactly as it is, and the package's own service is not enabled: nothing was moved or changed. To change over to the package, run: sudo systemctl disable --now coolercontrold; sudo rm %s; sudo systemctl daemon-reload; sudo systemctl enable --now coolercontrold. Your settings in /etc/coolercontrol stay and the package's service reads them. The same steps are in /usr/share/doc/coolercontrold/README.Debian. Nothing is moved for you."
